+### Act 26 pre-landing record — required, not ours to write
+
+Act 25 §7 (as amended by Act 26) requires, before landing, a verification record
+written by an office **other than the sponsor and other than the Clerk** to
+`$VICHE_STATE_ROOT/delivery/`. It must name the candidate commit, tree, parent,
+phase, exact commands and exits, and at least one content assertion with
+expected and actual values; a pass resting only on counts/suite exits is a fail.
+The reviewer pins the record digest and candidate to the board before landing.
+The landing must then be a fast-forward to exactly this candidate with no commit
+created at it.
+
+This office is the sponsor and therefore must not write or commission that
+record itself as a substitute for independent office verification. The Clerk
+should summon an eligible office (for example the Auditor `c1a0000b`) to write
+and pin it for `05d6158`/tree `5644e98`, using `tests/run-all.sh`, a focused
+gate check, and a content assertion such as the operative Act 25 heading match
+and the closure/recorded_by rejection. Until that record exists and is pinned,
+the candidate is not landable under Act 26. No merge or deployment is claimed.
